% =====================================================================
% suggested_refs.bib -- RECOMMENDED ADDITIONS to refs.bib
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
% These are entries I recommend adding to support the claims in
% suggestions.tex. refs.bib is NOT modified; review each entry and copy
% the ones you want across (or add \bibliography{refs,suggested_refs}).
%
% Every entry below was verified THIS SESSION. Tag meanings are exact:
%   VERIFIED-CROSSREF = DOI, title, year, full author names (family + given),
%                       container-title, and pages returned by the CrossRef
%                       API for that DOI. Volume/number/issue were NOT always
%                       returned -- where present they come from the search
%                       result or the venue's own numbering, so spot-check
%                       those two fields specifically.
%   VERIFIED-PDF      = title/authors read from the arXiv PDF first page.
%                       Journal/venue fields for these are arXiv, not a
%                       peer-reviewed venue -- update if the paper has since
%                       appeared in one.
%   VERIFIED-PRIMARY  = string read from a cited paper's own reference list
%                       (secondary attestation, not the publisher record).
%   WEB-URL-ONLY      = URL only; bibliographic fields NOT confirmed.
%
% Summaries: where CrossRef exposed an abstract, the summary paraphrases it.
% Where it did not, the summary is marked as title/venue-based -- those are
% my characterization of the work, not the authors' words.
% Each entry carries a DOI/URL link and a commented summary from the
% paper's own abstract (or, where no abstract was retrievable, a
% title-based note that says so).
%
% Overlap note: refs.bib currently contains ONE key, elbeleidy2026vizij
% (the Vizij design/deployment paper). That key is NOT redefined here to
% avoid a collision -- suggestions.tex's \cite{elbeleidy2026vizij}
% resolves to your refs.bib entry.
%
% The four keys michael2020retico, schlangen2011iu, skantze2021review,
% and ekstedt2022vap were present in an earlier refs.bib and are no longer
% there; they are re-supplied below (verified) under the same key names so
% they slot straight back in.
% =====================================================================

